@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+---
+id: task-002-implement-json-patch-applypatch-rfc-6902
+type: task
+title: "Implement JSON Patch applyPatch (RFC 6902)"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Request
+
+Implement JSON Patch (RFC 6902) with its six operations: `add`, `remove`, `replace`, `move`, `copy` and
+`test`. Export `applyPatch(document, patch)` from `src/index.ts`: it applies a patch (an array of
+operations) to a JSON document and returns the result as a new value, without mutating its input. It
+throws an error when the patch is invalid or when one of its operations fails.
+
+## Design
+
+Recorded in dl-003 (deep copy, new document), dl-004 (throwing on invalid patches and failed operations)
+and dl-005 (strict RFC 6902 semantics).
+
+## What was done
+
+- `test/apply-patch.test.ts`: written first. It covers the RFC 6902 appendix A examples, each operation,
+  the sequencing of operations, the no-mutation guarantee, invalid patches, failed operations, and a
+  member named `__proto__`. It was run before the implementation existed and failed, as expected (the
+  export did not exist).
+- `src/index.ts`: `applyPatch` and the exported type `JsonPatchOperation`, with doc comments. The
+  implementation reuses the pointer parser and member selection of `resolvePointer`, so both functions
+  accept the same pointers. `resolvePointer` now delegates its traversal to a shared helper with the same
+  behaviour.
+- `README.md`: a short usage section for `applyPatch`.
+
+## Verification
+
+- `npm test`: 72 of 72 tests pass (24 existing, 48 new).
+- `tsc -p tsconfig.json --noEmit` (TypeScript 5.9, strict mode, installed outside the repo and not added as
+  a dependency): no errors.
